																	<a href="/forum/t-13947554/the-imitation-blob#post-4849890">The Imitation Blob</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drtune" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7138420); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7138420&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608537399" alt="DrTune" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7138420)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drtune" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7138420); return false;" >DrTune</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608537263 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Dec 2020 07:54</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13947554/the-imitation-blob">The Imitation Blob</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849890">
									

<p>The Imatation Blob, found by the foundation playing in a small puddle, it normal behavior is freindly and curious, until introduced to a living creature via touch.</p>
<p>Upon being exposed to a living creature, the blob will trap the hand or foot of its victim with it's super sticky body then being to slowly swell in size until it capable of absorbing its victim into its body. At which point it will encompass them and until they have been completely dissolved into the blobs Body.</p>
<p>The Blob will then transform into a perfect replica of it's victim and adopt the victims mannerisms until it eats something else, at which point it will revert back to it's base form and resume normal behavior. Despite this The Blob has shown no need for food or water and can survive just fine without it.</p>
<p>That's how it behaved before incident (insert number here).</p>
<p>After multiple test on the Blob, D-Class testing was approved, The Blob behaved exactly the same throughout most of the test, up until D-Class (insert number here) was fully consumed.</p>
<p>However instead of adopting the D-Classes appearance and behavior, it remained in it's blob form for 10 minutes, studying itself, seemingly confused about it's own body.<br />
Afterwards The Blob transformed into a unknown creature and breached containment.</p>
<p>The Blob then proceeded to rampage through the site, taking the form of multiple creatures, many anomalous and previously unknown to the SCP foundation. Before a MTF squad managed to secure and recontain The Blob, it had killed multiple researchers and gaurds, and had even managed to absorb both an instance of SCP-939 and an instance of SCP-3199. Strangely, no D-Class were harmed during the breach, and The Blob seemed to target Security Gaurds and Reaserchers accompanied by D-Class above others.</p>
<p>The Blob now behaves extremely differently, it is aggressive and makes multiple attempts to breach containment every day. It has also begun to replicate 939 and use its ability to replicate human voices to communicate, although most of its vocabulary seems to consist of Explitives directed at Researchers.</p>
<p>This has led to the conclusion that instead of The Blob temporily replicating the physical appearence and behavior of the D-Class, it instead permanently replicate its behavior without replicating it's physical appearance, gaining sentience and a grudge against the foundation and it's personnel as well as a fondness and sense of comradery towards D-Class.</p>
<p>The Blob can also now control it's replication ability with relative ease. As such, it's containment procedures now require it be contained in a cell capable of containing as many different SCPs as possible, for it is unknown how many creatures The Blob is capable of replicating now.</p>
<p>In the event The Blob does breach containment, Security Gaurds are instructed to take as many D-class as possible into a secured intercom room. Then the Security Gaurds are instructed to threaten to terminate D-Class if The Blob does not return to containment, followed by terminate 1 D-Class every minute until The Blob returns to containment, a MTF squad arrives, or The Blob manages to gain access to the secured intercom room.</p>

							</div>

								
					
