<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No, I already have pages up.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> GoI Format</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> A &quot;password protected&quot; link to click to reveal the page</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Emma the fire-spewing Texas horned lizard fares better when placed by Cream the goose who lays golden eggs &#8212; so much better, in fact, that she grows beyond her expected size. When a robber stops by to steal the goose, he gets more than he bargained for.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Emma is a Texas horned lizard who shoots fire from her eyes instead of blood. She comes in clutching a gold ring, which is taken and sold, Wilson’s not realizing its importance. Emma then becomes smaller and more lethargic by the day, prompting concern from staff at Wilson's.</p>
<p>Cream is a goose who lays golden eggs which turn into normal eggs after a few hours. The page notes that there have been multiple inquiries and Cream is <em>not</em> up for adoption. When Cream gets transported past Emma’s terrarium for a checkup, Emma perks up and rushes to the front.</p>
<p>Wilson’s staff decide to put the two in enclosures next to each other and Emma starts healing with the proximity to gold. The two seem to like each other. Emma starts growing much larger than a horned lizard usually gets. Once she is large enough that her safety would no longer be a concern, Emma and Cream are placed together for short periods under close supervision. The two form a close bond, both showing signs of distress whenever they are separated.</p>
<p>In the email at the bottom, we learn of a Wilson’s overnight staff member hearing human screams along with distress calls from many of the animals. When they investigate, they find a robber who had tried to break into Cream's enclosure with a carrying cage. His hand is chewed off and he has severe burns all across his body. The lock to Emma's enclosure has melted open from the inside, but Emma is sitting inside near the wall that separates her from Cream. The robber is rushed to the hospital and the email suggests the web page be put under password protection in the future to avoid similar incidents — thus the password requirement at the beginning of the page.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Wilson's gets a sort-of dragon. Two animals make unlikely friends.</p>

